<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Loja, Ecuador</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Loja is a city in the southern highlands of Ecuador, the capital of the province of the same name. Founded by the Spanish around 1548, it was a centre for the gold mining and cinchona bark trade of the region. During the crisis of 1859, known as the 'terrible year', it briefly had its own government as Ecuador split into rival regimes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/loja-ecuador.jpg" alt="Loja, Ecuador" width="320" height="508" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David C. S. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Collage_Loja.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
